  "description": "A ring line (schema 27, ARCHITECTURE decision 49) on a loop of network track, edges 1 to 8 forward clockwise: straight edges of 1024 along the top, nodes 1 (2560, 1536) to 2 (3584, 1536) to 3 (4608, 1536), and along the bottom, 5 (4608, 3584) to 6 (3584, 3584) to 7 (2560, 3584), and at each corner one cubic edge with handles 1338 long that leaves one side's node along that side and arrives at the next side's along it, 3 to 4 (5632, 2560), 4 to 5, 7 to 8 (1536, 2560) and 8 to 1, each exactly 2048 long, the length of the grid's two links round the corner (edges join at a node only where they leave it in opposite directions, so a corner must be a curve). Alpha (3584, 512), Beta (6656, 2560), Gamma (3584, 4608) and Delta (512, 2560) each have one platform, the last 512 of the edge that leads clockwise into their node: Alpha e1 [512, 1024], Beta e3 [1536, 2048], Gamma e5 [512, 1024], Delta e7 [1536, 2048]. Clockwise a train stops at the node, anticlockwise at the platform's other end, 512 before it; either way from each to the next round the loop is 3072 units. A ring needs three stops or more and not the same station first and last (Short A-B and Back A-B-A cannot be one), and no patterns; making Ring one makes its counts even, down (5, 2, 1 to 4, 2, 0), and from then on it refuses patterns and stop lists that are not a ring, and keeps odd counts even (3 to 2). Setting a line that is not a ring to a line changes nothing. Ring plans with a crawl { acceleration 125, braking 100, topSpeed 1 }: a leg accelerates for 8 s, runs at 1 km/h and brakes for 10 s, 181.8 s, so 182; the lap the inner way is four legs, the last Delta to Alpha, and a minute at each stop, no terminal: 968 s, 17 minutes; the journey starts at Alpha's berth going clockwise, e1 forward 1024 (from its berth going back, e1 backward 512, the inner way round is much longer). At most 17 / 2 = 8 trains each way, 16 in all; with one each way the headway is 17 and every segment carries 1440 / 17 rounded up = 85 a day; a target of 5 runs 17 / 5 rounded up = 4 each way, 8, at 5 (288 a day). Inner and Outer stand at Alpha, Inner at its berth going clockwise (e1 forward 1024) and Outer at its berth going back (e1 backward 512, given an empty path that ends there, or it would run on to the end of its edge); Inner (the lower ID) runs the inner way, Alpha-Beta-Gamma-Delta-Alpha, Outer the outer way, Alpha-Delta-Gamma-Beta-Alpha. At 00:00 each way sends its train out (lastDispatch and outerLastDispatch 0): it leaves Alpha after the least dwell, 36 s (no terminal on a ring), and each stop is 182 + 60 s after the one before, never reversing: 0/36, 218/278, 460/520, 702/762, 944/944. The lap ends at 980 s, so at 00:17, before that minute's dispatch, both stand at Alpha's berths facing the way they came round, Outer's path still ending at 512.",
